Darth's post brings up the "things I'd like to see"
prompt/meme, for a new release, so here's my top
three:

1) Integration of large tiles/more colorful tiles
into the present circular conversion mechanism to
and from text encodings, so that a tileset, once
designed probably in an image processing program,
would be automatically portable to all NetHack
platforms via the text version of the encoding.

[I'd attempt this myself, but I'm back sleeping on
pavement, not a good time to do software
development.]

This is a _hard_ thing to do. Probably one of the
netpbm text formats would work well for a new
intermediate text format.

2) A relaxation/cleanup of the level-size code, so
that the player, via runtime defaults file option or
command line parameter, could choose to play in a
_huge_ level for each level not predesigned. This
would be unbalancing as heck, and probably locate
all the bad algorithm choices in the level layout
code very painfully, but to me, it would make the
game a lot more fun to be seeking the stairs to the
next level among a thousand rooms instead of among a
dozen.

3) [Duck and cover] Convert the source code to Java,
so that porting to different runtime environments
would be fairly painless.

